.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELL> void \fBcsmp::MathOperatorLHS\fP< dim, CELL >::GetOperands (const CELL< dim > & e_ref)\fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
getting data from the \fBElement\fP, \fBFace\fP, \fBInterFace\fP GetOperands fills a vector of material property matrices with the required values for later computation\&. These matrices always have the dimensions spatial-dimension^2 and they will hold either scalar, vector or tensor properties, depending on what kind of property the \fBOperand\fP is\&.

.PP
When the property is an element property, it will be put into the first vector entry MTRL[0]\&. 
.PP
Reimplemented in \fBcsmp::CVFEM_Upwind_NumIntegral_dNT_op_dN_dV< dim, CELL >\fP, \fBcsmp::Integral_dNT_op_dN_NT_v_dN_dV< dim, CELL >\fP, and \fBcsmp::Integral_NT_lhsop_N_dV< dim, CELL >\fP\&.
